<title>Turkmenistan: Turkmen May inflation 2.6 pct after 2.5 pct in Apr.</title>
<headline>Turkmen May inflation 2.6 pct after 2.5 pct in Apr.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan's consumer prices grew by 2.6 percent in May after a 2.5 percent rise in April, Sergei Bogomolov, head of the Central Bank's financial policy and research department, told Reuters.</p>
<p>    TURKMEN INFLATION		May '97	     May '96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month pct change	+2.6		  +2.5</p>
<p>Bogomolov said consumer prices in the first five months of this year grew by 17.2 percent.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 32 72 509410</p>
</text>
